  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed for both physical forward movement (troops, vehicles) and figurative progress (negotiations, research, plans). Often appears in news and formal contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {一歩|いっぽ}{前進|ぜんしん}する (to take one step forward)\n- {大|おお}きく{前進|ぜんしん}する (to make great progress)\n- {着実|ちゃくじつ}に{前進|ぜんしん}する (to advance steadily)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {進|すす}む: to advance, to go forward — general-purpose verb for moving ahead\n- {後退|こうたい}する: to retreat, to recede — the opposite of {前進|ぜんしん}する",
